       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. At that level the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral vasodilation. Overdose can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nPlease check whether this was a typo. Here are the usual options:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment:** 2.5 mg once daily.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg or 10 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you want a higher level of blood pressure control, adding a second agent from a different class is the usual approach. I can enter that order if you give me the drug and dose."
